        <div class="col-12"><button class="question-card question-moderate" data-answer-id="answer2">Q2 (Moderate): Build a generic class to store and print two values of different types.</button></div>
        <div class="col-12"><button class="question-card question-moderate" data-answer-id="answer3">Q3 (Moderate): Use generic constraints to allow only reference types in a repository class.</button></div>
        <div class="col-12"><button class="question-card question-moderate" data-answer-id="answer4">Q4 (Moderate): Write a delegate that performs arithmetic operation based on method assignment.</button></div>
        <div class="col-12"><button class="question-card question-moderate" data-answer-id="answer5">Q5 (Moderate): Demonstrate multicast delegate with two logging methods.</button></div>
        <div class="col-12"><button class="question-card question-moderate" data-answer-id="answer6">Q6 (Moderate): Use Func and Action with generics for reusable operations.</button></div>
        <div class="col-12"><button class="question-card question-moderate" data-answer-id="answer7">Q7 (Moderate): Create a generic list filter method using Predicate delegate.</button></div>
        <div class="col-12"><button class="question-card question-high" data-answer-id="answer8">Q8 (High): Build a generic event dispatcher using delegates and a type-safe payload.</button></div>
        <div class="col-12"><button class="question-card question-high" data-answer-id="answer9">Q9 (High): Implement covariance and contravariance using generic delegates.</button></div>
